onse, but I need to check if that's the full response object or just the data payload. If the backend controller is wrapping it as `{ success: true, data: { ... } }`, then there's definitely an extra layer of wrapping happening somewhere.\n\nLooking at the mobile app's expected structure, it seems like there should only be one `.data` level to reach `getAssetSummary`, but the way the backend is structured suggests there might be two levels. I'm trying to figure out if the service is returning the full GraphQL response with the nested `data` field, or if it's already unwrapped.\n\nActually, I'm probably overthinking this. The user said the app was working before, so the data unwrapping logic must have been fine. My styling changes to the colors and the `LinearGradient` component shouldn't affect data loading at all—unless the gradient is crashing and preventing the bars from rendering, which might make it look like the data isn't coming through.\n\nLet me reconsider what the user actually said: \"the CPU, memory, and disk information is now coming through.\" If \"now\" means \"no longer,\" then something I changed broke it. The only substantive changes were the theme colors and the `LinearGradient` implementation, so one of those must be the culprit. Now I should clean up the LinearGradient import since I reverted the UtilBar and it's no longer being used anywhere in the asset detail page.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":787,"cache_read_input_tokens":108902,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":787},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab312fcf-52d9-4bfd-b9f5-2b71e9f3b92d","uuid":"870d172c-71c5-4514-bcc7-b0deeb878ae3"}
