[2026-06-14 16:13:01] [claude-sdk] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01E8ypPvB4x5wCftBucay5CB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the issue. The backend's `createTicket` function builds the ticket subject as:\n\n```javascript\n\"subject\": ticketData.machineName + \" - \" + ticketData.subject\n```\n\nAnd it requires `addAssets.assetId`:\n\n```javascript\n\"addAssets\": {\n    \"assetId\": ticketData.assetId\n}\n```\n\nLooking at how the mobile's tickets page calls `createTicket`:\n\n```javascript\nawait createTicket({\n  subject: subject.trim(),\n  description: description.trim(),\n  accountId: superopsAccountId,\n  assetId: null,\n  machineName: null,\n});\n```\n\nThe problem is that both `machineName` and `assetId` are being passed as `null`. While the subject would become `\"null - Some subject\"`, the real culprit is likely the `addAssets: { assetId: null }` — SuperOps's GraphQL probably rejects null values in that field, causing the 500 error. The tickets page is creating account-level tickets rather than device-specific ones, so these fields aren't being populated.\n\nI need to decide whether to fix this in the backend by making `addAssets` conditional, or in the mobile app by not sending null values. The cleanest approach would be updating the backend's `createTicket` function to only include `addAssets` when there's an actual asset, and to handle the subject line gracefully when there's no machine name. Let me check how the web frontend handles this scenario.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":952,"cache_read_input_tokens":133727,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":952},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab