[2026-06-14 16:13:49] [claude-sdk] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01H9qRrAm2ifFPjVFncFn2RB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in the backend (`core-backend`). Here's what was wrong and what I changed:\n\n**Root cause:** The backend's `createTicket` service function always builds `addAssets: { assetId: ticketData.assetId }` in the SuperOps GraphQL mutation — even when `assetId` is `null`. SuperOps rejects that with a GraphQL error → 500. It also always prepended `machineName + \" - \"` to the subject, producing `\"null - Your subject\"` for account-level tickets.\n\n**Fix:** \n- `addAssets` is now only included when `assetId` is truthy\n- Subject line uses just the subject text when there's no `machineName`\n\n**You'll need to redeploy the backend to Heroku** for this to take effect. The changed file is `core-backend/domains/integrations/superops/superopsService.js`. Would you like me to commit and push it, or do you handle deploys separately?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":167,"cache_read_input_tokens":138161,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":167},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab312fcf-52d9-4bfd-b9f5-2b71e9f3b92d","uuid":"78bcb3d2-6733-41c7-a94d-b84c63589d7a"}
