[2026-06-14 16:33:52] [claude-sdk] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is building a Senturi mobile app (Expo + React Native) for their MSP (managed service provider) portal. This session focused on: bringing the web portal's branding/styling to the mobile app, fixing data display issues on the asset page, fixing ticket creation errors, fixing backup status display, cleaning up the profile page, adding modern UI upgrades (hero cards, search bars, polished profile), and most recently, adding a full-screen video background to the login page with a dark blue/green gradient overlay and white text/logo.\n\n   **Firm scope boundaries (DO NOT change without being asked)**:\n   - **NO signup / registration / Stripe / payment in the app** — accounts are provisioned by Senturi\n   - **Intercom** chat not yet added (needs native dev build)\n   - **BitDefender** AV status not surfaced (backend lacks read endpoint)\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Expo SDK 54** with React Native 0.81.5, Expo Router 6\n   - **react-native-appwrite** for auth (JS-only SDK, bundle ID `com.senturi.senturi`)\n   - **AppWrite**: endpoint `https://fra.cloud.appwrite.io/v1`, project `6830f7fd00056dd83fda`\n   - **Backend**: Express.js on Heroku (`https://senturi-backend-a66d7b816a1b.herokuapp.com`), API prefix `/api/v1/`\n   - **SuperOps GraphQL** via `graphql-request` — `.request()` auto-unwraps GraphQL `data` envelope; controllers wrap as `{ success, data: <gqlResult> }`\n   - **Comet backup** status codes: 5000-5999=success, 6000-6999=skipped, 7000-7999=failed\n   - **expo-linear-gradient** for gradient buttons/hero cards\n   - **expo-av** installed for video playback (login background)\n   - **Brand colors**: primary=#37aa7a, secondary=#2690bc, ink=#0c1d27, textDark=#1a2332, danger=#e1406e\n   - **Brand gradient**: `['#2690bc', '#37aa7a']` (90deg)\n   - Reanimated 4 needs `react-native-worklets` + babel plugin `react-native-worklets/plugin`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **`src/theme/theme.js`** — Complete design token system matching portal CSS variables\n     - Colors: ink=#0c1d27, danger=#e1406e, warning=#ffc107, success=#00b390, textDark=#1a2332, borderInput=#e8eaed, border=#f7f7f7, overlay=rgba(135,154,162,0.42)\n     - Gradients: brand=['#2690bc','#37aa7a'], brandReverse, progress=['#00a4b6','#00b390']\n     - Spacing: xs=4, sm=8, md=12, lg=16, xl=24, xxl=32, xxxl=40\n     - Radius: xs=4, sm=6, md=10, lg=16, xl=20, pill=999\n     - Shadow: card (1% opacity), elevated (8% opacity), button (blue-tinted), fab\n     - Typography: title (24/700/-0.5), heading (18/600), body (15/400), label (13/600), caption (12/400)\n\n   - **`src/components/ui.jsx`** — Shared components matching portal styling\n     - Button now uses LinearGradient for primary/secondary variants, supports `textStyle` prop\n     - Field has 14px/600 labels in textDark, 1.5px borderInput borders, #9ca3af placeholders\n     - Card uses radius.sm (6px), 1% opacity shadow\n     - EmptyState uses 2px dashed #dbe0e8 border\n     - Ghost/danger buttons remain flat (no gradient)\n\n   - **`app/(auth)/login.jsx`** — Currently white background, dark brand.png logo, icon-wrapped inputs, gradient sign-in button\n     - Uses brand.png (dark logo), white (#ffffff) background\n     - Green-tinted \"SECURE LOGIN\" badge\n     - Email input with mail-outline icon, password with lock-closed-outline + eye toggle\n     - Error displayed in pink row with alert-circle icon\n     - LinearGradient sign-in button with shadow.button\n     - **ABOUT TO BE REWRITTEN** with video background\n\n   - **`app/(app)/dashboard.jsx`** — Device list with gradient hero card + search\n     - LinearGradient hero (brand gradient) showing client name, Total/Online/Offline stats\n     - Search bar with search icon, clear button, filters by device name\n     - Device cards with blue-tinted icon background, status pill, chevron\n\n   - **`app/(app)/tickets.jsx`** — Ticket list with gradient hero card + search + create modal\n     - Blue gradient hero showing Total/Open/Closed stats\n     - Search bar filtering by subject or displayId\n     - FAB for new ticket creation\n     - Modal with handle indicator, gradient submit button\n\n   - **`app/(app)/backups.jsx`** — Backup history with gradient hero summary\n     - Teal-green gradient hero with last backup status badge pill, Total/Success/Failed stats\n     - Status range-based matching: Success (green), Failed (red), Running (blue), Skipped (gray)\n     - Job cards with tinted status icons and status badge pills\n\n   - **`app/(app)/profile.jsx`** — Polished profile with support links and branded footer\n     - 88px gradient avatar with initials\n     - Account card: Client, Role, Status (phone number and Technical card removed)\n     - Support card: \"Contact support\" (mailto:support@senturi.io), \"Visit senturi.io\"\n     - Footer: faded brand.png logo (15% opacity), version from expo-constants, \"Simple. Safe. Secure.\"\n\n   - **`app/(app)/_layout.jsx`** — Tab bar with refined styling\n     - 88px height, 11px/600 tab labels, letter-spacing 0.3\n     - Flat header (no shadow), 17px/700 title with -0.3 letter-spacing\n\n   - **`app/_layout.jsx`** — Root layout with StatusBar style=\"auto\" (was \"light\")\n\n   - **`app/inactive.jsx`** — Inactive account screen with icon in tinted circle background\n\n   - **`app/asset/[assetId].jsx`** — Asset detail with plain View utilization bars (no LinearGradient)\n     - UtilBar uses plain View with backgroundColor (green/warning/danger based on percentage)\n     - Data unwrapping has deeper fallbacks: `sData?.getAssetSummary ?? sData?.data?.getAssetSummary`\n     - Patch details unwrapping: `pData?.getAssetPatchDetails ?? pData?.data?.getAssetPatchDetails`\n     - Tile icons in tinted wrapper backgrounds\n     - Modal with handle indicator, portal overlay color\n\n   - **`src/utils/format.js`** — Fixed metricValue and cometStatus\n     - `metricValue()` now uses `Number()` coercion instead of strict `typeof === 'number'` check\n     - `cometStatus()` now uses range-based checking (5000-5999=Success, 6000-6999=Skipped, 7000-7999=Failed)\n\n   - **`core-backend/domains/integrations/superops/superopsService.js`** — Fixed createTicket\n     - `addAssets` only included when `ticketData.assetId` is truthy\n     - Subject line: `machineName ? machineName + \" - \" + subject : subject`\n     - **Needs redeployment to Heroku** for fix to take effect\n\n   - **`app.json`** — Splash/icon backgrounds updated to #0c1d27\n\n   - **Assets**: `assets/brand-white.png` and `assets/brand.png` copied from core-frontend\n\n4. Errors and Fixes:\n\n   - **LinearGradient percentage widths in UtilBar**: LinearGradient component didn't render properly with percentage widths on device. Fixed by reverting to plain View with backgroundColor.\n   \n   - **metricValue too strict**: Only accepted JavaScript `number` type, but SuperOps GraphQL fields can return strings or objects with string values. Fixed by using `Number()` coercion: `const n = Number(v); return Number.isNaN(n) ? null : n;`\n   \n   - **Asset data unwrapping incomplete**: Added deeper fallback paths (`data.getAssetSummary` and `data.data.getAssetSummary`) to handle potential nesting differences.\n   \n   - **Ticket creation 500 error**: Backend always sent `addAssets: { assetId: null }` for account-level tickets. Fixed backend to conditionally include addAssets only when assetId is truthy. Also fixed subject line to not prepend \"null - \". Backend needs redeployment.\n   \n   - **All backups showing yellow/attention**: cometStatus() only matched 3 exact codes (5000, 5001, 7002). Changed to range-based: 5000-5999=Success, 6000-6999=Skipped, 7000-7999=Failed.\n   \n   - **Stray HTML in login page**: First rewrite of login had a stray `<input>` HTML element and duplicate blocks. Fixed in second write.\n   \n   - **Unused imports**: Cleaned up unused LinearGradient import from asset detail, unused Ionicons from login.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Traced SuperOps backend response shapes by reading controller, service, and GraphQL queries to understand exact data unwrapping needs\n   - Identified that `graphql-request`'s `.request()` auto-unwraps GraphQL `data` envelope vs `.rawRequest()` which doesn't\n   - Discovered web portal only creates tickets from asset detail page (always has assetId), explaining why the bug only manifests in mobile's account-level ticket creation\n   - Explored Comet API status code ranges to properly categorize backup statuses\n\n6. All User Messages:\n   - \"Take out the century word underneath the brand on the login page. Century spelled S-E-N-T-U-R-I.\"\n   - \"Make the logo larger?\"\n   - \"Look at the portal on the front end. Uh, core dash front end. And bring over its styles and fonts and colors. And make the app look like that.\"\n   - \"Can you refresh the app for me?\"\n   - \"On the asset page, the CPU, memory, and disk information is now coming through. Can you fix that?\" (meaning NOT coming through)\n   - \"In the CPU, memory, and disk still aren't coming through on the assets page. You can just change the color to green instead of using any kind of gradient if that solves it.\"\n   - \"On the login page, can we switch to a darker logo and then make everything white? more modern-looking?\"\n   - \"From the tickets page I'm not able to add a new ticket. It says request failed with status code 500. Please check the super ops integration and make sure it's hooked up, or let me know if we need the .env config file brought over from the previous file system.\"\n   - \"Well, I do all the backups on the back of history page. Show yellow or needs attention flags or tags.\"\n   - \"On the profile page, we need to remove the technical block entirely that contains the SuperOps account ID and the AppWrite ID, the customer doesn't need to see that.\"\n   - \"On the profile page, you can also remove their phone number.\"\n   - \"Is there anything else that we need to add to the application to make it look more modern? This is going to go on our website, and I want to look at want it to look as cool as possible.\"\n   - \"Okay, I'm going to log in page. It would be really cool if you could pull a IT-related video or small business-related video, place that as the background, full width and full height, um, overlay a our dark blue color on it with a splash of the brighter green gradient, just to give it kind of a modern feel. And then you can bring back the logo to be white and the text on top of it to be white as well.\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **Backend redeployment needed**: The createTicket fix in `core-backend/domains/integrations/superops/superopsService.js` needs to be deployed to Heroku\n   - **Video background login page**: Currently in progress (expo-av installed, stock video sources identified, implementation not yet started)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   The user's most recent request is to add a video background to the login page. Specifically:\n   - Pull an IT-related or small business-related stock video\n   - Place it as full-width, full-height background\n   - Overlay the dark blue color (#0c1d27) with a splash of the brighter green gradient\n   - Switch logo back to white (brand-white.png)\n   - Make all text white\n   \n   So far: `expo-av` has been installed for video playback. A web search was performed to find free stock video sources (Pexels, Pixabay). The actual implementation of the video background login page has NOT been started yet.\n\n   The current login page at `app/(auth)/login.jsx` has a white background with dark brand.png logo, which needs to be completely reworked.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Implement the video background login page. This requires:\n   1. Find a suitable free stock video URL (IT/cybersecurity/tech themed) from Pexels or Pixabay that can be loaded via URL\n   2. Rewrite `app/(auth)/login.jsx` to use `expo-av`'s `Video` component as a full-screen background\n   3. Add a dark blue overlay with green gradient splash on top of the video\n   4. Switch back to `brand-white.png` (white logo)\n   5. Make all text elements white\n   6. Keep the same form structure (icon inputs, gradient button, badge)\n\n   User's exact words: \"pull a IT-related video or small business-related video, place that as the background, full width and full height, um, overlay a our dark blue color on it with a splash of the brighter green gradient, just to give it kind of a modern feel. And then you can bring back the logo to be white and the text on top of it to be white as well.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/andrewprice/.claude/projects/-Users-andrewprice-senturi-core-senturi-mobile/ab312fcf-52d9-4bfd-b9f5-2b71e9f3b92d.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab312fcf-52d9-4bfd-b9f5-2b71e9f3b92d","uuid":"e4061f15-7eb6-4d67-8e59-54c6f545476a","timestamp":"2026-06-14T21:33:52.457Z","isSynthetic":true}
