[2026-06-14 17:04:55] [claude-sdk] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01QAeGZedPps25k3TCU9jpvJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user says it doesn't look like it's moving. My approach of using marginTop on brandWrap might not be working as I expected with the flex-end layout. Let me rethink this.\n\nWith `justifyContent: 'flex-end'` on heroSection, the SafeAreaView content is pushed to the bottom. Adding marginTop to brandWrap makes the content block taller, but the SafeAreaView might be constrained by the heroSection's minHeight, so it might not actually move.\n\nActually, the issue might be that the SafeAreaView has `edges={['top']}`, which adds padding for the safe area at the top. \n\nThe SafeAreaView wraps the content and gets pushed to the bottom via flex-end, but to move the logo higher on screen, I need to either increase the hero section's minHeight or adjust the padding and margins differently. Increasing minHeight would make the section taller, but that might not be the right solution.\n\nThe best approach is to add more paddingBottom to the heroContent to push the content up from the bottom of the hero section, rather than changing the flex alignment. The current paddingBottom is around 32, so I'll increase it significantly to something like 80 or more, and remove the marginTop on brandWrap since that wasn't helping.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25,"cache_read_input_tokens":90569,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab312fcf-52d9-4bfd-b9f5-2b71e9f3b92d","uuid":"5803ea76-31bd-4af8-a187-5170163494f8"}
